items.grow_notes:
The Ethiopian Shashamane provides a high-energy mental and body high that’s perfect for daytime activities.

It grows in the central highlands of Ethiopia at an altitude ranging from 800-1,200 meters. The buds usually have a combination of lemon and a spicy taste that’s similar to tea masala.

The phenotype tastes and smells like freshly harvested green mango. Here’s a short video that explains the characteristics of the Ethiopian Shashamane phenotype;

